                    <div class="flex flex-col">
                        <div class="h-7 flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10">
                            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/45">04 · Evidence</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-center py-10">
                            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white leading-none">Evidence the other side can check without you.</h2>
                        <p class="mt-5 text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-white/90 leading-snug">The behavioral system of record for autonomous work.</p>
                        <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-white/70 uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">Who acted, which agent, which model, under which policy.</p>
                        <p class="mt-8 text-lg text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
                            Every entry is hash-chained at the boundary, before anything reaches a provider, and held outside the reach of the thing being recorded. Altering one link breaks every link after it, and an auditor recomputes the chain offline, without us in the room. Your provider's log lives on their infrastructure and is read through their console. In a dispute that involves them, it is theirs, not yours.
                        </p>
                        <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-sm text-white/40 leading-relaxed">
                            The gateway and the ledger are open source.
                            <a href="https://github.com/kydehq/gateway" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-white/60 hover:text-white underline underline-offset-4 decoration-white/20 hover:decoration-white/60 transition-colors">github.com/kydehq/gateway →</a>
                        </p>
                        <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-[11px] text-white/35 leading-relaxed">
                            Ed25519-signing each entry with your own keys, which proves authorship rather than order, is an Enterprise capability.
